[metadata] {"type": "create", "filePath": "/app/output/final_report.html", "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Global Fuel Price Trends & Policy Impact Analysis (2020–2026)</title>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.0/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
<style>
  :root {
    --primary: #1a3a5c;
    --accent: #e8641a;
    --accent2: #2a7fc9;
    --accent3: #27ae60;
    --accent4: #8e44ad;
    --bg: #f4f6f9;
    --card: #ffffff;
    --border: #dce3ec;
    --text: #1d2530;
    --muted: #5a6578;
    --danger: #c0392b;
    --warning: #e67e22;
    --success: #27ae60;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* HEADER */
  .report-header {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0d2137 0%, #1a3a5c 50%, #234c78 100%);
    color: #fff; padding: 48px 60px 40px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .report-header::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; top: -60px; right: -60px;
    width: 300px; height: 300px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.04); pointer-events: none;
  }
  .report-header .badge {
    display: inline-block; background: var(--accent); color: #fff;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 3px; margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .report-header h1 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .report-header .subtitle { font-size: 15px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75); max-width: 660px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .header-meta { display: flex; gap: 32px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .header-meta span { font-size: 12px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); }
  .header-meta strong { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); }

  /* LAYOUT */
  .container { max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 32px; }
  .section { margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .section-header { margin-bottom: 20px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border); display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; }
  .section-number { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: 1px; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .section-header h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); }
  .section-objective { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 20px; font-style: italic; max-width: 820px; }

  /* KPI CARDS */
  .kpi-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .kpi-card {
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px 18px; position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .kpi-card::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px;
  }
  .kpi-card.blue::after { background: var(--accent2); }
  .kpi-card.orange::after { background: var(--accent); }
  .kpi-card.green::after { background: var(--accent3); }
  .kpi-card.purple::after { background: var(--accent4); }
  .kpi-card.red::after { background: var(--danger); }
  .kpi-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.8px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .kpi-value { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .kpi-desc { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); }

  /* CHARTS */
  .chart-grid-2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .chart-grid-3 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 24px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .chart-card {
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px; position: relative;
  }
  .chart-card.full { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .chart-title { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .chart-subtitle { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .chart-container { position: relative; }

  /* TABLES */
  .data-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .data-table th {
    background: var(--primary); color: #fff; font-weight: 600; font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; padding: 10px 12px; text-align: left;
  }
  .data-table td { padding: 9px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .data-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .data-table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #f7f9fc; }
  .data-table .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .data-table .badge-pill {
    display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 12px; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600;
  }
  .badge-high { background: #fde8e8; color: var(--danger); }
  .badge-medium { background: #fef3e2; color: var(--warning); }
  .badge-low { background: #e8f5e9; color: var(--success); }
  .badge-veryhigh { background: #ede7f6; color: var(--accent4); }

  /* INSIGHTS */
  .insight-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .insight-box {
    background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 18px; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent2);
  }
  .insight-box.warn { border-left-color: var(--warning); }
  .insight-box.success { border-left-color: var(--success); }
  .insight-box.danger { border-left-color: var(--danger); }
  .insight-box h4 { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 6px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }
  .insight-box p { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text); }

  /* FINDINGS */
  .findings-list { list-style: none; }
  .findings-list li {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 36px 1fr; gap: 16px; align-items: start;
    padding: 18px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .findings-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .finding-num {
    width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--primary);
    color: #fff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .finding-body h4 { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .finding-body p { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text); }
  .finding-body .tag {
    display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.8px;
    text-transform: uppercase; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--accent); color: #fff; margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .finding-body .tag.policy { background: var(--accent2); }
  .finding-body .tag.risk { background: var(--danger); }
  .finding-body .tag.equity { background: var(--accent3); }

  /* BAR CHART INLINE */
  .bar-inline { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .bar-track { flex: 1; height: 8px; background: #e9ecef; border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
  .bar-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 4px; }

  /* STAT CALLOUT */
  .stat-callout {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #e8f4fd 0%, #d6eaf8 100%);
    border: 1px solid #aed6f1; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 24px;
    margin-bottom: 24px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .stat-callout .stat { text-align: center; }
  .stat-callout .stat-val { font-size: 32px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary); }
  .stat-callout .stat-lbl { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.8px; }
  .stat-callout .divider { width: 1px; height: 50px; background: #aed6f1; }
  .stat-callout .narrative { flex: 1; font-size: 13px; color: var(--text); min-width: 200px; }

  /* FOOTER */
  .report-footer { background: var(--primary); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.6); padding: 24px 60px; font-size: 12px; margin-top: 48px; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .kpi-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
    .chart-grid-2, .chart-grid-3 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .insight-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .container { padding: 20px 16px; }
    .report-header { padding: 32px 20px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ HEADER -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="badge">Policy Analysis Report</div>
  <h1>Global Fuel Price Trends &amp; Policy Impact Analysis<br>2020 – 2026</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">A comprehensive trend analysis of retail fuel prices across 84 countries, examining the interplay between Brent Crude benchmarks, taxation, subsidies, and regional economic conditions over a six-year period.</div>
  <div class="header-meta">
    <span><strong>Coverage:</strong> 84 Countries · 7 Regions</span>
    <span><strong>Period:</strong> Jan 2020 – Apr 2026 (weekly)</span>
    <span><strong>Observations:</strong> 27,468 records</span>
    <span><strong>Audience:</strong> Energy Policy Analysts</span>
    <span><strong>Published:</strong> April 2026</span>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ SECTION 1: OVERVIEW -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">Section 01</span>
    <h2>Global Fuel Price Overview</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="section-objective">High-level summary statistics for petrol, diesel, and LPG prices across the full 2020–2026 period, with Brent Crude as the global baseline. All prices in USD per liter unless noted.</p>

  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card blue">
      <div class="kpi-label">Avg Petrol Price</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$2.28</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">USD/liter · global mean (2020–2026)<br>Range: $0.01 – $6.78</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card orange">
      <div class="kpi-label">Avg Diesel Price</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$2.13</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">USD/liter · global mean (2020–2026)<br>Range: $0.01 – $6.24</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card green">
      <div class="kpi-label">Avg LPG Price</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$1.71</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">USD/liter · global mean (2020–2026)<br>Consistently ~25% below petrol</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card purple">
      <div class="kpi-label">Brent Crude Range</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$48–$130</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">USD/barrel · period extremes<br>Min: Apr 2020 · Max: Mar 2022 / 2026</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card red">
      <div class="kpi-label">Avg Tax on Fuel</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">26.8%</div>
      <div class="kpi-desc">Global mean tax % of retail price<br>Ranges by income level: 21–35%</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-grid-2">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <div class="chart-title">Annual Average Fuel Prices by Type</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle">USD/liter · Global mean across all 84 countries</div>
      <div class="chart-container" style="height:240px;">
        <canvas id="chartAnnualFuel"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <div class="chart-title">Brent Crude Annual Average (USD/barrel)</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle">Global benchmark alongside retail petrol trend</div>
      <div class="chart-container" style="height:240px;">
        <canvas id="chartBrentAnnual"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight-grid">
    <div class="insight-box">
      <h4>Price Trajectory</h4>
      <p>Global average petrol prices more than doubled from <strong>$1.08/liter</strong> at their 2020 trough (week of April 27) to <strong>$2.78/liter</strong> at the 2022 peak (March–April 2022), driven by Brent Crude rising from $47.97 to $130.00/barrel over the same period.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-box success">
      <h4>Fuel Type Spread</h4>
      <p>Diesel averages <strong>6.5% below petrol</strong> globally ($2.13 vs $2.28/liter), while LPG sits <strong>25% below petrol</strong> ($1.71/liter). This spread is consistent across years, suggesting structural pricing differentials independent of crude movements.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-box warn">
      <h4>2026 Acceleration</h4>
      <p>Preliminary 2026 data (Jan–Apr) shows petrol averaging <strong>$2.65/liter</strong> — the highest annual figure in the dataset — with Brent at $123.75/barrel, suggesting continued upward pressure heading into the second half of 2026.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-box danger">
      <h4>Extreme Price Disparity</h4>
      <p>The gap between the world's most expensive fuel market (Hong Kong: <strong>$5.54/liter</strong>) and cheapest (Venezuela: <strong>$0.016/liter</strong>) is <strong>346x</strong> — almost entirely a function of subsidy depth and tax policy rather than proximity to crude production.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ SECTION 2: TEMPORAL TRENDS -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-number">Section 02</span>
    <h2>Temporal Price Trends &amp; Volatility</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="section-objective">Weekly and annual price dynamics for all three fuel types, with special focus on the COVID-19 demand shock (2020) and the 2022 energy crisis. Quantifies the Brent-to-retail correlation and year-by-year volatility.</p>

  <div class="stat-callout">
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-val">1.000</div>
      <div class="stat-lbl">Brent–Petrol<br>Pearson r</div>
    </div>
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-val">1.000</div>
      <div class="stat-lbl">Brent–Diesel<br>Pearson r</div>
    </div>
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-val">−46%</div>
      <div class="stat-lbl">Brent drop<br>Jan→Apr 2020</div>
    </div>
    <div class="divider"></div>
    <div class="stat">
      <div class="stat-val">+171%</div>
      <div class="stat-lbl">Brent rise<br>Apr 2020→Mar 2022</div>
    </div>
    <div class="narrative">
      <strong>Correlation note:</strong> The Pearson correlation between weekly Brent Crude and global-average retail petrol/diesel prices is <strong>r = 1.000</strong> (computed from 327 weekly data points, 2020–2026). This near-perfect correlation reflects the dataset methodology — retail prices are derived from a multi-stage pipeline incorporating crude as a primary input. While this confirms the structural link between commodity and pump prices, analysts should note that individual country-level pass-through rates vary significantly based on subsidy regimes and tax structures (see Section 4).
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-card full" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="chart-title">Weekly Global Average Retail Prices vs. Brent Crude (2020–2026)</div>
    <div class="chart-subtitle">Global mean petrol, diesel, and LPG prices (USD/liter, left axis) overlaid with Brent Crude (USD/barrel ÷ 50, right axis for visual alignment). 327 weekly data points.</div>
    <div class="chart-container" style="height:320px;">
      <canvas id="chartWeeklyAll"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-grid-2">
    <div class="chart-card">
      <div class="chart-title">Petrol Price Volatility by Year</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle">Standard deviation of global avg weekly petrol price (USD/liter)</div>
      <div class="chart-container" style="height:220px;">
        <canvas id="chartVolatility"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card">
      <div class="chart-title">Year-over-Year Price Change (Petrol %)</div>
      <div class="chart-subtitle">Annual average vs. prior year — global mean</div>
      <div class="chart-container" style="height:220px;">
        <canvas id="chartYoY"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="insight-grid">
    <div class="insight-box danger">
      <h4>COVID-19 Demand Shock (Q1–Q2 2020)</h4>
      <p>Brent Crude collapsed from <strong>$70.53/barrel</strong> (March 2, 2020) to <strong>$47.97/barrel</strong> (April 27, 2020) — a <strong>32% decline in 8 weeks</strong>. Global average petrol fell from $1.51 to $1.02/liter. The COVID shock is the sharpest single-quarter price drop in the 2020–2026 window.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-box warn">
